{
  "_comment": [
    "MCP stdio handshake cases (mcp-update-plan PR-3 §3.0-§3.1). Synthetic and read-only: no case runs a tool.",
    "Each case runs in a fresh server process. `send` items are JSON values sent as one line each, or",
    "{\"raw\": \"...\"} / {\"raw_bytes_hex\": \"...\"} for lines that aren't valid JSON.",
    "`expect` holds one expectation per target: `graph_mem` (asserted by spec/requests/mcp_protocol_compat_spec.rb)",
    "and `reference` (Memory 2.0.0, checked by script/mcp_compat/compare.rb; null when the case is graph_mem-only).",
    "An expectation gives `replies` (the exact number of reply lines) and `messages`, matched by `id` (null-id",
    "replies in order): `error_code`, or `result` (subset match) and `result_has` (keys that must exist).",
    "Every stdout line must be a JSON-RPC 2.0 message. `divergence` says why graph_mem and the reference may differ;",
    "`changes_in` names the plan step that changes graph_mem's answer.",
    "Reference expectations come from the v2.0.0 code (plan §0b) and were confirmed against",
    "@modelcontextprotocol/server-memory 2.0.0 with server/core 2.3.1 (the tag's lockfile) on 2026-10-24."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "initialize 2025-03-26 is echoed",
      "send": [
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "initialize", "params": {"protocolVersion": "2025-03-26", "capabilities": {}, "clientInfo": {"name": "mcp-compat", "version": "0"}}}
      ],
      "expect": {
        "graph_mem": {"replies": 1, "messages": [{"id": 1, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-03-26"}}]},
        "reference": {"replies": 1, "messages": [{"id": 1, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-03-26"}}]}
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "initialize 2025-11-25 is echoed, with serverInfo",
      "send": [
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "initialize", "params": {"protocolVersion": "2025-11-25", "capabilities": {}, "clientInfo": {"name": "mcp-compat", "version": "0"}}}
      ],
      "expect": {
        "graph_mem": {"replies": 1, "messages": [{"id": 1, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-11-25"}, "result_has": ["serverInfo", "capabilities"]}]},
        "reference": {"replies": 1, "messages": [{"id": 1, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-11-25"}, "result_has": ["serverInfo", "capabilities"]}]}
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "initialize capabilities: no subscribe or listChanged; instructions present",
      "send": [
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "initialize", "params": {"protocolVersion": "2025-11-25", "capabilities": {}, "clientInfo": {"name": "mcp-compat", "version": "0"}}}
      ],
      "expect": {
        "graph_mem": {"replies": 1, "messages": [{"id": 1, "result": {"capabilities": {"resources": {"subscribe": false, "listChanged": false}, "tools": {"listChanged": false}}}, "result_has": ["instructions"]}]},
        "reference": null
      },
      "divergence": "Server-specific: Memory implements resource subscriptions and list-changed notifications; graph_mem doesn't."
    },
    {
      "name": "initialize 2026-07-28 gets 2025-11-25",
      "send": [
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "initialize", "params": {"protocolVersion": "2026-07-28", "capabilities": {}, "clientInfo": {"name": "mcp-compat", "version": "0"}}}
      ],
      "expect": {
        "graph_mem": {"replies": 1, "messages": [{"id": 1, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-11-25"}}]},
        "reference": {"replies": 1, "messages": [{"id": 1, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-11-25"}}]}
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "initialize \"9\" gets 2025-11-25",
      "send": [
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "initialize", "params": {"protocolVersion": "9", "capabilities": {}, "clientInfo": {"name": "mcp-compat", "version": "0"}}}
      ],
      "expect": {
        "graph_mem": {"replies": 1, "messages": [{"id": 1, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-11-25"}}]},
        "reference": {"replies": 1, "messages": [{"id": 1, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-11-25"}}]}
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "server/discover with a 2026-07-28 envelope",
      "send": [
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 7, "method": "server/discover", "params": {"_meta": {"io.modelcontextprotocol/protocolVersion": "2026-07-28", "io.modelcontextprotocol/clientCapabilities": {}, "io.modelcontextprotocol/clientInfo": {"name": "mcp-compat", "version": "0"}}}}
      ],
      "expect": {
        "graph_mem": {"replies": 1, "messages": [{"id": 7, "result": {"supportedVersions": ["2026-07-28"]}}]},
        "reference": {"replies": 1, "messages": [{"id": 7, "result": {"supportedVersions": ["2026-07-28"], "resultType": "complete"}, "result_has": ["capabilities", "_meta"]}]}
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "server/discover claiming 2027-01-01",
      "send": [
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 7, "method": "server/discover", "params": {"_meta": {"io.modelcontextprotocol/protocolVersion": "2027-01-01", "io.modelcontextprotocol/clientCapabilities": {}, "io.modelcontextprotocol/clientInfo": {"name": "mcp-compat", "version": "0"}}}}
      ],
      "expect": {
        "graph_mem": {"replies": 1, "messages": [{"id": 7, "result": {"supportedVersions": ["2026-07-28"]}}]},
        "reference": {"replies": 1, "messages": [{"id": 7, "error_code": -32022}]}
      },
      "divergence": "graph_mem (the official SDK) answers discover with its supported versions whatever the envelope claims; Memory answers -32022. Either way the client then picks a version both support."
    },
    {
      "name": "server/discover with an envelope missing clientCapabilities",
      "send": [
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 7, "method": "server/discover", "params": {"_meta": {"io.modelcontextprotocol/protocolVersion": "2026-07-28", "io.modelcontextprotocol/clientInfo": {"name": "mcp-compat", "version": "0"}}}}
      ],
      "expect": {
        "graph_mem": {"replies": 1, "messages": [{"id": 7, "result": {"supportedVersions": ["2026-07-28"]}}]},
        "reference": {"replies": 1, "messages": [{"id": 7, "error_code": -32602}]}
      },
      "divergence": "graph_mem (the official SDK) answers discover without clientCapabilities in the envelope; Memory refuses it with -32602."
    },
    {
      "name": "tools/list with a 2026-07-28 envelope and no initialize is served",
      "send": [
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "method": "tools/list", "params": {"_meta": {"io.modelcontextprotocol/protocolVersion": "2026-07-28", "io.modelcontextprotocol/clientCapabilities": {}, "io.modelcontextprotocol/clientInfo": {"name": "mcp-compat", "version": "0"}}}}
      ],
      "expect": {
        "graph_mem": {"replies": 1, "messages": [{"id": 2, "result_has": ["tools", "resultType", "ttlMs", "cacheScope"]}]},
        "reference": {"replies": 1, "messages": [{"id": 2, "result_has": ["tools", "resultType", "ttlMs", "cacheScope"]}]}
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "discover, then initialize 2025-11-25, then tools/list (the auto-mode fallback path)",
      "send": [
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "server/discover", "params": {"_meta": {"io.modelcontextprotocol/protocolVersion": "2026-07-28", "io.modelcontextprotocol/clientCapabilities": {}, "io.modelcontextprotocol/clientInfo": {"name": "mcp-compat", "version": "0"}}}},
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "method": "initialize", "params": {"protocolVersion": "2025-11-25", "capabilities": {}, "clientInfo": {"name": "mcp-compat", "version": "0"}}},
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "notifications/initialized"},
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "method": "tools/list"}
      ],
      "expect": {
        "graph_mem": {"replies": 3, "messages": [{"id": 1, "result": {"supportedVersions": ["2026-07-28"]}}, {"id": 2, "error_code": -32601}, {"id": 3, "error_code": -32602}]},
        "reference": {"replies": 3, "messages": [{"id": 1, "result_has": ["supportedVersions"]}, {"id": 2, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-11-25"}}, {"id": 3, "result_has": ["tools"]}]}
      },
      "divergence": "After server/discover, graph_mem (the official SDK) keeps the process in the 2026-07-28 era and refuses the legacy initialize and the tools/list after it; Memory falls back in-process. The TS client isn't affected: in auto mode it probes in a sibling process."
    },
    {
      "name": "malformed lines: parse error, batch, missing jsonrpc, primitive",
      "send": [
        {"raw": "{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":"},
        [{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "method": "ping"}],
        {"id": 3, "method": "ping"},
        42
      ],
      "expect": {
        "graph_mem": {"replies": 4, "messages": [{"id": null, "error_code": -32700}, {"id": 2, "result": {}}, {"id": 3, "error_code": -32600}, {"id": null, "error_code": -32600}]},
        "reference": {"replies": 0, "messages": []}
      },
      "divergence": "graph_mem (the official SDK) answers malformed lines with JSON-RPC errors and serves a one-element batch; the TS SDK drops them silently. Both keep serving."
    },
    {
      "name": "an unknown notification gets no reply",
      "send": [
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "notifications/mcp_compat_unknown"},
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 9, "method": "ping"}
      ],
      "expect": {
        "graph_mem": {"replies": 1, "messages": [{"id": 9, "result": {}}]},
        "reference": {"replies": 1, "messages": [{"id": 9, "result": {}}]}
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "tools/call with \"id\": null is refused, not run",
      "send": [
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "initialize", "params": {"protocolVersion": "2025-11-25", "capabilities": {}, "clientInfo": {"name": "mcp-compat", "version": "0"}}},
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "notifications/initialized"},
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": null, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "get_current_time", "arguments": {}}},
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 5, "method": "ping"}
      ],
      "expect": {
        "graph_mem": {"replies": 3, "messages": [{"id": 1, "result_has": ["protocolVersion"]}, {"id": null, "error_code": -32600}, {"id": 5, "result": {}}]},
        "reference": {"replies": 2, "messages": [{"id": 1, "result_has": ["protocolVersion"]}, {"id": 5, "result": {}}]}
      },
      "divergence": "Neither runs it: graph_mem answers -32600 (like the Ruby SDK 1.8.1); the TS SDK drops the line silently."
    },
    {
      "name": "tools/call without an id is a notification: no reply, not run",
      "send": [
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "initialize", "params": {"protocolVersion": "2025-11-25", "capabilities": {}, "clientInfo": {"name": "mcp-compat", "version": "0"}}},
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "notifications/initialized"},
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "get_current_time", "arguments": {}}},
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 5, "method": "ping"}
      ],
      "expect": {
        "graph_mem": {"replies": 2, "messages": [{"id": 1, "result_has": ["protocolVersion"]}, {"id": 5, "result": {}}]},
        "reference": {"replies": 2, "messages": [{"id": 1, "result_has": ["protocolVersion"]}, {"id": 5, "result": {}}]}
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "resources/subscribe is not offered",
      "send": [
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "initialize", "params": {"protocolVersion": "2025-11-25", "capabilities": {}, "clientInfo": {"name": "mcp-compat", "version": "0"}}},
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "notifications/initialized"},
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "method": "resources/subscribe", "params": {"uri": "memory_graph"}}
      ],
      "expect": {
        "graph_mem": {"replies": 2, "messages": [{"id": 1, "result_has": ["protocolVersion"]}, {"id": 4, "error_code": -32601}]},
        "reference": null
      },
      "divergence": "Server-specific: Memory implements resource subscriptions; graph_mem advertises subscribe: false."
    },
    {
      "name": "an invalid UTF-8 object key, then a ping",
      "send": [
        {"raw_bytes_hex": "7b226a736f6e727063223a22322e30222c226964223a312c226d6574686f64223a2270696e67222c22706172616d73223a7b22ff223a317d7d"},
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "method": "ping"}
      ],
      "expect": {
        "graph_mem": {"replies": 2, "messages": [{"id": null, "error_code": -32700}, {"id": 2, "result": {}}]},
        "reference": {"replies": 2, "messages": [{"id": 1, "result": {}}, {"id": 2, "result": {}}]}
      },
      "divergence": "graph_mem refuses invalid UTF-8 with -32700 (like the Ruby SDK 1.8.1); Node decodes the byte as U+FFFD and answers the ping. Both keep serving."
    },
    {
      "name": "tools/call with an invalid UTF-8 tool name, then a ping",
      "send": [
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "initialize", "params": {"protocolVersion": "2025-11-25", "capabilities": {}, "clientInfo": {"name": "mcp-compat", "version": "0"}}},
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "notifications/initialized"},
        {"raw_bytes_hex": "7b226a736f6e727063223a22322e30222c226964223a34322c226d6574686f64223a22746f6f6c732f63616c6c222c22706172616d73223a7b226e616d65223a2273796e74682dff222c22617267756d656e7473223a7b7d7d7d"},
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 5, "method": "ping"}
      ],
      "expect": {
        "graph_mem": {"replies": 3, "messages": [{"id": 1, "result_has": ["protocolVersion"]}, {"id": 42, "error_code": -32603}, {"id": 5, "result": {}}]},
        "reference": {"replies": 3, "messages": [{"id": 1, "result_has": ["protocolVersion"]}, {"id": 42, "error_code": -32602}, {"id": 5, "result": {}}]}
      },
      "divergence": "graph_mem can't echo the invalid name back and answers -32603 with the id (Ruby SDK 1.8.2, #629); Node decodes the byte as U+FFFD and answers -32602 \"Tool synth-\uFFFD not found\". Both keep serving."
    }
  ]
}
